      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_3rkav6gepw",
          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "column": 0,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The arc of the program"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Toggle Headings unfold to reveal content."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_g8wp8bk9k4",
          "type": "accordion",
          "v": 1,
          "column": 1,
          "fields": {
            "items": [
              {
                "question": "01 Why before the How Start with what matters. +",
                "answer": {
                  "type": "doc",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "We begin with the values that hold this up: confidence, preparation, competence, and care for each other. Participants form small accountability groups of three and get a simple worksheet to start sizing up their own neighborhood. This is where the relationships start."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "question": "02 Knowing your neighbors The art of the knock on the door. +",
                "answer": {
                  "type": "doc",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Who on your block needs checking on in a crisis? Who has medical equipment, large animals, or particular vulnerabilities? Who has skills, tools, or a generator to share? We learn from the Neighborhood Villaging Project about what it actually takes to "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "know",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " the people who live near you — including the conversation you've been meaning to have."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "question": "03 Walking the neighborhood Map the place you actually live. +",
                "answer": {
                  "type": "doc",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Participants bring their assessments to the group. We plan and walk site visits together — walking the streets to find risks, evacuation routes, water sources, gathering points, and resources. Every neighborhood is different. You learn it with your feet."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "question": "04 The basics Water. Power. First aid. Wellbeing. +",
                "answer": {
                  "type": "doc",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Dedicated sessions on water, power, and building practical first aid kits that go beyond the standard checklist. We cover psychological first aid, hygiene, and the often-overlooked realities of staying well during sustained disruption. Not just for one bad day — for two weeks of bad days."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "question": "05 The drill What does recovery actually look like? +",
                "answer": {
                  "type": "doc",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "How do you work with government agencies, nonprofits, and each other to get back on your feet? We run a full practice scenario — fire, flood, prolonged outage, civic disruption — then we sit down and pull out what worked, what didn't, and where the plan needs to get better. The drill is where the plan meets reality."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "question": "06 The capstone Present your neighborhood's plan. +",
                "answer": {
                  "type": "doc",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Each participant presents their finished Community Resiliency Plan — ideally alongside a neighbor they walked the program with. We close with a Resiliency Dinner — because "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "the relationships you built in this program are the resilience.",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " Everything else is scaffolding."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "exclusive": false,
            "openFirst": false,
            "faqSchema": false
          }
        }
      ]
    },
